{"candidateAnswer":"His Uncle","evidence":"[D12:2 | 1:12 pm on 3 August, 2023] Dave: Hey Calvin, I understand the stress of getting a car serviced. Fixing cars is like therapy for me. Growing up working on cars with my dad, refurbishing them gives me a sense of fulfillment.\n[D12:4 | 1:12 pm on 3 August, 2023] Dave: Yeah, definitely! I have fond memories of working on cars with my dad as a kid. We spent one summer restoring an old car. It was hard work, but seeing the end result and knowing that we did it together was really satisfying.\n[D26:6 | 8:25 pm on 25 October, 2023] Dave: Thanks, Calvin! It's always been my thing. My dad took me to my first car show when I was 10, and I was wow-ed! I was hooked and wanted to learn more. Now I'm an automotive engineer and it's crazy to think that something so powerful and cool can be made from small parts.","itemId":"urn:uuid:c8cb885e-5ce2-5164-b1ce-477754678505","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:f2368227cec0b98d27dbbe39c107cc04a4b3762caafe0b5d1313532ba042e5fe","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Who inspired Dave's passion for car engineering?","referenceAnswer":"His Dad","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"f2368227cec0b98d27dbbe39c107cc04a4b3762caafe0b5d1313532ba042e5fe"}}]}